The problem I see and have seen with WinDOS based development is that
people tend to program non-standard C which results in non-portable code.
If you program standard conforming then the platform question is just
relevant for the OS specific parts. Nethack has the OS specific parts
put in their own OS specific directories. The biggest part of the game
is OS *independent*. Separating OS specific I/O from the beginning and
creating an abstraction layer helps.

